dpkg-reconfigure-noninteractive(8) -- wrapper to run `dpkg-reconfigure` non-interactively
=============================================

<!--
# Copyright (C) 2012 - 2025 ENCRYPTED SUPPORT LLC <adrelanos@whonix.org>
# See the file COPYING for copying conditions.
-->

## SYNOPSIS
`dpkg-reconfigure-noninteractive` [option]s pkg-name

## Description
Simple wrapper that

* sets environment variables for non-interactive use,
* prevents daemons from restarting during reconfiguration,

then forwards all arguments to `dpkg-reconfigure`.

Under the non-interactive frontend `dpkg-reconfigure` does not ask the
debconf questions again. It re-applies the answers already stored in the
debconf database, so this is the right tool to regenerate a package's
configuration from values seeded earlier (for example with
`debconf-set-selections`) without any prompt.

Unlike `dpkg-noninteractive` no `--force-conf*` option is added, because
`dpkg-reconfigure` does not accept dpkg conffile options.

## Examples
`sudo dpkg-reconfigure-noninteractive tzdata`

`sudo dpkg-reconfigure-noninteractive keyboard-configuration`

